=back

Returns boolean: true on success or false on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.2.0.


=head1 ENUMERATIONS

Every enumerator is exported as a constant sub.

=head2 SDL_SystemTheme

System theme.

=over

=item SDL_SYSTEM_THEME_UNKNOWN = 0 - Unknown system theme

=item SDL_SYSTEM_THEME_LIGHT = 1 - Light colored system theme

=item SDL_SYSTEM_THEME_DARK = 2 - Dark colored system theme

=back

=head2 SDL_DisplayOrientation

Display orientation values; the way a display is rotated.

=over

=item SDL_ORIENTATION_UNKNOWN = 0 - The display orientation can't be determined

=item SDL_ORIENTATION_LANDSCAPE = 1 - The display is in landscape mode, with the right side up, relative to portrait mode

=item SDL_ORIENTATION_LANDSCAPE_FLIPPED = 2 - The display is in landscape mode, with the left side up, relative to portrait mode

=item SDL_ORIENTATION_PORTRAIT = 3 - The display is in portrait mode

=item SDL_ORIENTATION_PORTRAIT_FLIPPED = 4 - The display is in portrait mode, upside down

=back

=head2 SDL_FlashOperation

Window flash operation.

=over

=item SDL_FLASH_CANCEL = 0 - Cancel any window flash state

=item SDL_FLASH_BRIEFLY = 1 - Flash the window briefly to get attention

=item SDL_FLASH_UNTIL_FOCUSED = 2 - Flash the window until it gets focus

=back

=head2 SDL_ProgressState

Window progress state

=over

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_INVALID = -1 - An invalid progress state indicating an error; check SDL_GetError()

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_NONE = 0 - No progress bar is shown

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_INDETERMINATE = 1 - The progress bar is shown in a indeterminate state

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_NORMAL = 2 - The progress bar is shown in a normal state

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_PAUSED = 3 - The progress bar is shown in a paused state

=item SDL_PROGRESS_STATE_ERROR = 4 - The progress bar is shown in a state indicating the application had an error

=back

=head2 SDL_GLAttr

An enumeration of OpenGL configuration attributes.

=over

=item SDL_GL_RED_SIZE = 0 - the minimum number of bits for the red channel of the color buffer; defaults to 8.

=item SDL_GL_GREEN_SIZE = 1 - the minimum number of bits for the green channel of the color buffer; defaults to 8.

=item SDL_GL_BLUE_SIZE = 2 - the minimum number of bits for the blue channel of the color buffer; defaults to 8.

=item SDL_GL_ALPHA_SIZE = 3 - the minimum number of bits for the alpha channel of the color buffer; defaults to 8.

=item SDL_GL_BUFFER_SIZE = 4 - the minimum number of bits for frame buffer size; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_DOUBLEBUFFER = 5 - whether the output is single or double buffered; defaults to double buffering on.

=item SDL_GL_DEPTH_SIZE = 6 - the minimum number of bits in the depth buffer; defaults to 16.

=item SDL_GL_STENCIL_SIZE = 7 - the minimum number of bits in the stencil buffer; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_ACCUM_RED_SIZE = 8 - the minimum number of bits for the red channel of the accumulation buffer; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_ACCUM_GREEN_SIZE = 9 - the minimum number of bits for the green channel of the accumulation buffer; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_ACCUM_BLUE_SIZE = 10 - the minimum number of bits for the blue channel of the accumulation buffer; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_ACCUM_ALPHA_SIZE = 11 - the minimum number of bits for the alpha channel of the accumulation buffer; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_STEREO = 12 - whether the output is stereo 3D; defaults to off.

=item SDL_GL_MULTISAMPLEBUFFERS = 13 - the number of buffers used for multisample anti-aliasing; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_MULTISAMPLESAMPLES = 14 - the number of samples used around the current pixel used for multisample anti-aliasing.

=item SDL_GL_ACCELERATED_VISUAL = 15 - set to 1 to require hardware acceleration, set to 0 to force software rendering; defaults to allow either.

=item SDL_GL_RETAINED_BACKING = 16 - not used (deprecated).

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_MAJOR_VERSION = 17 - OpenGL context major version.

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_MINOR_VERSION = 18 - OpenGL context minor version.

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_FLAGS = 19 - some combination of 0 or more of elements of the SDL_GLContextFlag enumeration; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_PROFILE_MASK = 20 - type of GL context (Core, Compatibility, ES). See SDL_GLProfile; default value depends on platform.

=item SDL_GL_SHARE_WITH_CURRENT_CONTEXT = 21 - OpenGL context sharing; defaults to 0.

=item SDL_GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB_CAPABLE = 22 - requests sRGB-capable visual if 1. Defaults to -1 ("don't care"). This is a request; GL drivers might not comply!

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_RELEASE_BEHAVIOR = 23 - sets context the release behavior. See SDL_GLContextReleaseFlag; defaults to FLUSH.

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_RESET_NOTIFICATION = 24 - set context reset notification. See SDL_GLContextResetNotification; defaults to NO_NOTIFICATION.

=item SDL_GL_CONTEXT_NO_ERROR = 25

=item SDL_GL_FLOATBUFFERS = 26

=item SDL_GL_EGL_PLATFORM = 27

=back

=head2 SDL_HitTestResult

Possible return values from the SDL_HitTest callback.

=over

=item SDL_HITTEST_NORMAL = 0 - Region is normal. No special properties.

=item SDL_HITTEST_DRAGGABLE = 1 - Region can drag entire window.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_TOPLEFT = 2 - Region is the resizable top-left corner border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_TOP = 3 - Region is the resizable top border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_TOPRIGHT = 4 - Region is the resizable top-right corner border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_RIGHT = 5 - Region is the resizable right border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_BOTTOMRIGHT = 6 - Region is the resizable bottom-right corner border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_BOTTOM = 7 - Region is the resizable bottom border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_BOTTOMLEFT = 8 - Region is the resizable bottom-left corner border.

=item SDL_HITTEST_RESIZE_LEFT = 9 - Region is the resizable left border.

=back



